  "text": "We are given a **cube with edge length 6 cm**, and **9 dots are placed on each face**, each at the **midpoint of a square**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understand the geometry\n\nEach face of the cube has **9 dots**, and each dot is at the **midpoint of a square**. So:\n\n- Each face has 9 dots.\n- There are **6 faces** in total.\n- Each dot is shared between two faces (since a dot is on a square, and a square belongs to two adjacent faces).\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Total number of dots\n\n$$\n6 \\text{ faces} \\times 9 \\text{ dots per face} = 54 \\text{ dots}\n$$\n\nThese 54 dots are connected **pairwise**, forming a **network of line segments**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Total length of all line segments\n\nTo find the **total length of all the line segments**, we need to count how many segments there are and their lengths.\n\nEach **dot is connected to 4 other dots**, forming a **network of 54 dots**, and each connection corresponds to a **straight line**.\n\nSo, total number of **line segments** is:\n\n$$\n54 \\times 4 = 216\n$$\n\nEach **line segment** connects two dots at the **midpoint of a square**. The distance between two midpoints of adjacent squares can be calculated.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Distance between midpoints of adjacent squares\n\nLet’s think geometrically: suppose the cube has side length 6 cm. The **midpoint** of a square on a face is 3 cm from each corner.\n\nNow, consider two adjacent squares on adjacent faces.\n\n- The distance between the midpoints of these two squares is:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{(3)^2 + (3)^2} = \\sqrt{18} = 4.2426 \\text{ cm}\n$$\n\nSo, each **line segment** between two adjacent dots has length **≈ 4.2426 cm**\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Total length of all line segments\n\n$$\n216 \\text{ segments} \\times 4.2426 \\text{ cm/segment} \\approx 924.26 \\text{ cm}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{924} \\text{ cm}\n$$",
